.TH VIDWIZARD 1 "2026-08-20" "vidwizard 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vidwizard \- high-quality command-line video edits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vidwizard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.IR inputs ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vidwizard
applies common video-editor operations from the command line using the FFmpeg
libraries.
Defaults keep quality high (libx264 CRF 16, Rec.709 grayscale, max-compressed
32-bit PNG) and use every logical CPU core.
Options and input paths may appear in any order.
Several operations on one command run as one sequential filter graph
(for example crop, then grayscale, then speed) without extra flags.
Ranges are optional; omit them to apply an effect to the whole clip.
With no arguments,
.B vidwizard
prints the same help as
.B \-h
and exits 0.
.PP
Time ranges are
.I START-END,START-END,...
An open end
.RI ( 10- ", " 1:00- )
runs to the end of the clip.
An open start
.RI ( \-20 )
runs from time zero.
Times may be seconds
.RI ( 10.5 ),
.I MM:SS
or
.IR HH:MM:SS
(fractions allowed).
Empty ranges mean the whole timeline.
.PP
.B \-\-reverse
buffers the selected frames in memory (fine for short clips; huge files
may need a lot of RAM).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
Never used for verbose mode.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " PATH"
Single output file or directory.
One input plus a file path uses that exact name.
Several inputs plus a file path warn and write
.I outstem_instem.ext .
A directory (existing, trailing slash, or created) receives default-named
outputs.
.TP
.BR \-\-grayscale [ =RANGES ]
High-quality Rec.709 grayscale.
Optional ranges apply the effect only in those windows.
.TP
.BR \-\-explode [ =RANGES ]
Write lossless 32-bit RGBA PNG frames with zlib level 9 and mixed prediction.
Names are
.I stem_0001.png
with zero-pad width taken from the frame count (20 frames → 01..20).
.TP
.BI \-\-cut " RANGES"
Extract each range as its own video
.RI ( stem_cut_01.ext ).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " FACTOR[:RANGES]"
Forward speed multiplier (for example 1.5, 2, 2.75).
Audio is kept in sync with pitch-preserving
.B atempo
unless
.B \-\-mute
is given.
Optional ranges speed only those windows; the rest stays 1×.
.TP
.BI \-\-crop " GEOM[:RANGES]"
Crop
.I WxH+X+Y
or
.IR W:H:X:Y .
.I WxH
or
.I W:H
crops from the centre.
Ranged crop zooms that rectangle during the windows and keeps the original
frame size.
.TP
.BR \-\-reverse [ =RANGES ]
Reverse the whole video, or reverse listed windows in place.
.TP
.BR \-\-mute [ =RANGES ]
Drop all audio, or silence the listed windows (audio stream kept).
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs " N"
Worker/encoder threads.
Default: all logical cores.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Extra progress on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-log-file " PATH"
Also write diagnostics to
.IR PATH .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including help and version.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error or no usable inputs.
.TP
.B 2
One or more inputs failed to process.
.SH EXAMPLES
Grayscale a file (writes
.IR clip_gray.mp4 ):
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-grayscale
.RE
.PP
Explode frames:
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-explode
.RE
.PP
Cut two parts:
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-cut 10-20,1:00-1:30
.RE
.PP
Speed up two windows by 2.75×:
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-speed 2.75:10-20,30-40
.RE
.PP
Crop the centre 640×360:
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-crop 640x360
.RE
.PP
Sequential ops (one graph, no ranges needed):
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-crop 640x360 \-\-grayscale \-\-speed 2
.RE
.PP
Grayscale from five minutes to the end:
.RS
.B vidwizard clip.mp4 \-\-grayscale 5:00-
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Written for the vidwizard project.
